course: dictionary
lesson: 12069
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word cleanse is a good example. «Cleanse the cut with water» is about clean skin, but in a church or Bible story, cleanse means to make someone pure again.
explain: Read the words around cleanse to choose the right meaning. A cut and a plaster point to first aid. Sin and God point to faith. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Cleanse is a verb, so it describes an action, and its word form changes: cleanses, cleansed, cleansing. «Mia cleansed the scratch yesterday» uses the past tense. Read the sentence aloud to hear which form fits best.
fact: Cleanse is a verb. It means to clean something thoroughly, or to make something pure.
fact: «Cleanse» can mean cleaning a wound to stop germs, as in «Cleanse the cut with water.»
fact: A cleanser is a product, such as soap for the face, that cleans the skin.
fact: In church and the Bible, «cleanse» means to make someone free from sin or guilt. Psalm 51 asks God to «cleanse me from my sin».
fact: In history, «ethnic cleansing» is a term for a terrible crime, where a whole group of people is driven out or killed because of who they are.
exercise: «Cleanse the cut with water before you put on the plaster.» What does cleanse mean here? | To make the water go cold | To put a plaster on very tightly | *To clean thoroughly, to stop germs | To cut the water into pieces
exercise: «Cleanse me from my sin.» In this sentence, what does cleanse mean? | To dirty something on purpose | To count backwards from ten | *To make someone pure and free from sin or guilt | To fall asleep quickly
exercise: What does «cleanse the air» mean? | To make it louder | To hide it from view | *To remove harmful or unwanted things from it | To warm it up
test: Cleanser is a noun. What is a cleanser? | A loud noise in the night | *Soap or a product that cleans the skin | A person who is very rude | A type of bird that sings at dawn
test: Which form of cleanse fits this sentence? «Yesterday, Mia ___ the scratch.» | cleanses | cleanse | *cleansed | cleansing
exam: In «cleanse me from my sin», what kind of cleansing is meant? | *To make someone pure and free from guilt | To paint a room | To wash the dirty dishes | To remove stains from clothes
